How "no value" reads:

- [1mAbsent[0m — nothing to report: not applicable ([2mworktree[0m on a branch-only
  row), not requested this run (the envelope's [2mcollected[0m records what was),
  or determined-empty (no PR, no lock, not integrated).
- [1m[2mnull[0m[0m — requested but not determined: a task timed out, the branch was
  too stale for the expensive checks, or a forge fetch failed. This is the
  JSON form of the table's [2m·[0m placeholder.

jq treats absent and [2mnull[0m identically in path expressions, so filters need
no null checks; [2mhas()[0m distinguishes the two when it matters.

Envelope fields:

 Field   Type                            Description                            
 ────── ────── ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── 
 [2mschema[0m number Format version; always [2m2[0m                                         
 [2mrepo[0m   object [2m{default_branch, forge}[0m — the branch every [2mdefault_branch[0m object 
               measures against (absent when detection failed), and forge       
               metadata derived from the primary remote (absent when no remote  
               URL parses; see repo object)                                     
 [2mcollec[0m object [2m{ci, summary}[0m — which gated fact families this run requested, so 
 [2mted[0m           an absent [2mpr[0m/[2mchecks[0m/[2msummary[0m reads as "not requested" rather than 
               "none"                                                           
 [2mitems[0m  array  One object per row: a worktree, a local branch, or a remote-only 
               branch                                                           

