 [2mremote[0m   string Local remote name; present on [2mrepo.forge[0m, absent from [2mpr.repo[0m 

[32mstate values[0m

The single highest-priority state describing the branch's relation to the 
default branch; absent when none applies (a normal up-to-date branch). Each 
value is one Default-branch symbol — see Default branch for the symbol and the 
full meaning of each value ([2m"is_main"[0m, [2m"orphan"[0m, [2m"empty"[0m, [2m"integrated"[0m, 
[2m"would_conflict"[0m, [2m"same_commit"[0m, [2m"diverged"[0m, [2m"ahead"[0m, [2m"behind"[0m).

[32mintegration reasons[0m

[2mdefault_branch.integration.reason[0m records which check matched. Checks run 
cheapest-first and the first match wins. JSON-only — every reason renders as the
 same [2m⊂[0m:

     Value                                  Meaning                             
 ────────────── ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── 
 [2m"same_commit"[0m  Branch HEAD is the default branch's commit                      
 [2m"ancestor"[0m     Branch HEAD is an ancestor of the default branch, which has     
                moved past it                                                   
 [2m"no_added_chan[0m The three-dot diff ([2mmain...branch[0m) is empty — no file changes   
 [2mges"[0m           beyond the merge-base                                           
 [2m"trees_match"[0m  Different history, but the branch's tree is identical to the    
                default branch's                                                
 [2m"merge_adds_no[0m The branch has changes, but merging them leaves the default     
 [2mthing"[0m         branch's tree unchanged (e.g. a squash merge where the target   
                advanced on other files)                                        
 [2m"patch_id_matc[0m The branch's squashed diff matches a single commit on the       
 [2mh"[0m             default branch (e.g. a GitHub/GitLab squash merge)              

[32mreview states[0m

[2mpr.review[0m is one of [2m"changes_requested"[0m, [2m"pending"[0m, [2m"draft"[0m, [2m"approved"[0m, absent 
when the forge reports no review signal. The CI status section is the single 
source: its table maps the colored values, and the notes below it cover [2m"draft"[0m 
and [2m"approved"[0m. The vocabulary matches Claude Code's statusline [2mpr.review_state[0m 
field.

