A JSON Schema for the envelope is published at
worktrunk.dev/schema/list-v2.json.
It describes what [2mwt[0m writes, so a field the absence rule can omit is
optional there rather than required-and-null.

[32mSchema 1[0m

The original bare-array format — one object per row, no envelope — and the
default while [2m[list] json-schema[0m is unset. It is on its way out: [2mwt config[0m
update[2m adopts [0m= 2[2m, a future release flips the default, and a later one[0m
removes schema 1. Its fields all have a schema-2 home:

                 Schema 1                               Schema 2                
 ──────────────────────────────────────── ───────────────────────────────────── 
 [2mbranch[0m                                   [2mbranch[0m                                
 [2mpath[0m                                     [2mworktree.path[0m                         
 [2mkind[0m                                     the row's shape — a [2mworktree[0m object   
                                          means [2m"worktree"[0m, no [2mworktree[0m object  
                                          means [2m"branch"[0m                        
 [2mcommit.sha[0m, [2m.short_sha[0m, [2m.message[0m         [2mhead.sha[0m, [2m.short_sha[0m, [2m.subject[0m        
 [2mcommit.timestamp[0m (Unix)                  [2mhead.committed_at[0m (RFC 3339 UTC)      
 [2mworking_tree.staged[0m, [2m.modified[0m,          [2mworktree.changes.*[0m                    
 [2m.untracked[0m, [2m.renamed[0m, [2m.deleted[0m, [2m.diff[0m                                          
 [2moperation_state[0m [2m"conflicts"[0m              [2mworktree.changes.conflicted[0m           
 [2moperation_state[0m [2m"rebase"[0m, [2m"merge"[0m, …     [2mworktree.operation[0m                    
 [2mmain_state[0m                               [2mdisplay.state[0m                         
 [2mintegration_reason[0m                       [2mdefault_branch.integration.reason[0m     
                                          (snake_case, and it reports           
                                          [2m"same_commit"[0m rather than folding it  
                                          into [2mmain_state[0m)                      
 [2mmain.ahead[0m, [2m.behind[0m, [2m.diff[0m               [2mdefault_branch.ahead[0m, [2m.behind[0m, [2m.diff[0m  
 [2mremote.name[0m, [2m.branch[0m, [2m.ahead[0m, [2m.behind[0m    [2mupstream.remote[0m, [2m.branch[0m, [2m.ahead[0m,     
                                          [2m.behind[0m                               
 [2mworktree.state[0m                           [2mworktree.locked[0m, [2m.prunable[0m,           
                                          [2m.duplicate_branch[0m, [2m.branch_mismatch[0m — 
                                          independent, so they co-occur         
 [2mworktree.reason[0m                          [2mworktree.locked.reason[0m,               
                                          [2mworktree.prunable.reason[0m              
 [2mworktree.detached[0m                        [2mworktree.detached[0m                     
 [2mis_main[0m, [2mis_current[0m, [2mis_previous[0m         [2mworktree.main[0m, [2m.current[0m, [2m.previous[0m    
 [2mci.status[0m                                [2mchecks.status[0m, plus the shapes        
                                          described under checks object         
 [2mci.source[0m, [2mci.stale[0m                      [2mchecks.source[0m, [2mchecks.stale[0m           
 [2mci.number[0m, [2mci.url[0m, [2mci.review_state[0m       [2mpr.number[0m, [2mpr.url[0m, [2mpr.review[0m          
 [2mci.repo[0m, [2mci.repo_url[0m                     [2mpr.repo[0m, [2mpr.repo.url[0m                  
 [2mrepo[0m, [2mrepo_url[0m                           the envelope's [2mrepo.forge[0m,            
                                          [2mrepo.forge.url[0m                        
 [2murl[0m, [2murl_active[0m                          [2mdev_server.url[0m, [2mdev_server.listening[0m  
 [2msummary[0m, [2mvars[0m                            [2msummary[0m, [2mvars[0m                         
 [2mstatusline[0m, [2msymbols[0m, [2mcolumns[0m             [2mdisplay.statusline[0m, [2mdisplay.symbols[0m,  
                                          [2mdisplay.columns[0m                       

The envelope's [2mrepo.default_branch[0m and [2mcollected[0m have no schema-1 equivalent, 
and schema 2 separates "nothing to report" from "not determined" — see How "no 
value" reads.

Missing a field that would be generally useful? Open an issue at 
https://github.com/max-sixty/worktrunk.

